## Summary
This article helps when a document is sent to the printer but nothing prints, or the printer shows as offline.

## Symptoms
- The user clicks Print but nothing comes out
- A job stays in the print queue
- The printer shows "Offline"

## Cause
Common causes are a stuck job in the print queue, the Print Spooler service (the program that manages print jobs) having stopped, a lost cable or Wi-Fi connection, or the wrong printer being selected.

## Resolution
1. Check that the printer is on, has paper and ink, and is connected by cable or Wi-Fi.
2. Open Settings > Bluetooth & devices > Printers & scanners. Select the printer, click "Open print queue" and cancel any stuck jobs.
3. Press Windows key + R, type `services.msc` and press Enter. Find "Print Spooler", right-click it and select "Restart".
4. Make sure the correct printer is set as default in Printers & scanners.
5. Print a test page from the printer's properties.

## Verification
The test page prints and the user can print their own document.

## Prevention
Do not click Print repeatedly when a large document is slow to start. Keep the printer driver updated.

## Escalation
Escalate if the Print Spooler keeps stopping, or if several users have the same problem on the same printer. Include the printer name, the error message and the steps you tried.

